# CP2K twin (offline oracle) — Berry-phase dipole of bulk Si (GPW class)
# Pairs with regressions/gpw/periodic-berry-gpw/REFERENCE.md.
# Never executed at ctest/regression time (offline pin only).
#
# Matched algorithm twin of ATV cpu::gpw::BerryPolarization (KSV / modern
# theory of polarization). CP2K evaluates the same observable via
# &MOMENTS PERIODIC T (Resta Γ-limit / Berry-phase dipole) on Quickstep
# GPW: GTH + Gaussian MOLOPT basis, PADE LDA, orthorhombic BCT diamond Si.
# Absolute phases may differ by a quantum; the symmetry pins
# (half-quantum lattice membership for the centrosymmetric cell, ASR
# Z* = 0 under sublattice displacement) are basis-independent and are
# the scientific content of the regression.
#
# Wall twin: time this single ENERGY job (1 MPI × fixed OMP) — same SCF
# class as the ATV string-mesh SCF that feeds Berry.

&GLOBAL
  PROJECT si_periodic_berry_gpw
  RUN_TYPE ENERGY
  PRINT_LEVEL MEDIUM
&END GLOBAL
&FORCE_EVAL
  METHOD Quickstep
  &DFT
    BASIS_SET_FILE_NAME BASIS_MOLOPT
    POTENTIAL_FILE_NAME GTH_POTENTIALS
    &QS
      EPS_DEFAULT 1.0E-10
    &END QS
    &MGRID
      CUTOFF 80
      REL_CUTOFF 40
    &END MGRID
    &SCF
      SCF_GUESS ATOMIC
      EPS_SCF 1.0E-7
      MAX_SCF 60
    &END SCF
    &XC
      &XC_FUNCTIONAL PADE
      &END XC_FUNCTIONAL
    &END XC
    &KPOINTS
      SCHEME MONKHORST-PACK 2 2 2
    &END KPOINTS
    &PRINT
      &MOMENTS
        PERIODIC T
        REFERENCE COM
      &END MOMENTS
    &END PRINT
  &END DFT
  &SUBSYS
    &CELL
      # BCT diamond Si orthorhombic: a/√2, a/√2, a with a = 5.43 Å
      ABC 3.83959 3.83959 5.43
      PERIODIC XYZ
    &END CELL
    &COORD
      Si  0.00000  0.00000  0.00000
      Si  1.91980  1.91980  2.71500
      Si  1.91980  0.00000  1.35750
      Si  0.00000  1.91980  4.07250
      # displaced twin: move atom 2 by +0.02 * C = (0, 0, 0.1086)
    &END COORD
    &KIND Si
      BASIS_SET DZVP-MOLOPT-GTH
      POTENTIAL GTH-PADE-q4
    &END KIND
  &END SUBSYS
&END FORCE_EVAL
